="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["cloud-native","cpp","database","distributed-database","distributed-sql","distributed-sql-database","high-performance","kubernetes","multi-cloud","multi-region","scale-out","sql"],"visibility":"public","forks":1201,"open_issues":7608,"watchers":9958,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Jira Link: [DB-4534](https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-4534)\r\n\r\nYBM cluster hit soft memory limits, causing degradation in YSQL latencies and follower lag for certain tablets. \r\nPerforming a rolling-restart fixed the cluster for a bit (follower lag came down), but the memory use continued to rise and caused soft-memory limit on all nodes, rendering the cluster inoperable. Even after scaling up the instances, the same behavior was observed. However, the cluster recovered automatically. \r\nWe need to investigate what happened so that we can appropriately take action on the cluster to scale it to the appropriate size.\n\n[DB-4534]: https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-4534?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/15407/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/15407/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"not_planned"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":8642417490,"node_id":"CE_lADOBlCVUc5etTtNzwAAAAIDINNS","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/events/8642417490","actor":{"login":"yugabyte-ci","id":17281578,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjgxNTc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17281578?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yugabyte-ci","html_url":"https://g